{"title":"USA TST","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>USA TST</b>, or USA Team Selection Test, is a test administered to the top approximately 30 scorers on the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.evanchen.cc/faq-rules.html#CR-1\">USA TSTST</a>. The results are used to determine the team that is sent to the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO\">IMO</a> (although it is not the sole determining factor). Nowadays, it consists of 6 problems over 2 days, like the USAMO. The questions (especially since 2015) are noticeably harder than corresponding problems on the USAMO. \n</p>\n<table style=\"border:thin solid black;padding:10px;float:right;margin:10px;background:#fff;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"border:thin solid gray;text-align:center;background:#ccf;\"><b>USA TST</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Region</b>: USA\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Type</b>: Proof\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AoPS_Wiki:Competition_ratings\" title=\"AoPS Wiki:Competition ratings\">Difficulty</a></b>: 7-9.5\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Difficulty Breakdown:</b>\n<p><u>Problem 1/4/7</u>: 7<br /><u>Problem 2/5/8</u>: 8<br /><u>Problem 3/6/9</u>: 9.5\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=USA_TST&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018112447\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.010 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.018 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 24/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 659/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 99/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/50000